config BR2_PACKAGE_BHP_PRESENCE_SENSOR
	bool "bhp-presence-sensor"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	help
	  Build the experimental house-panel PIR input module and the
	  board's inert experiment overlays listed by
	  BHP_BOARD_PRESENCE_OVERLAYS in config/boards/<BR2_BHP_BOARD_ID>.env.

	  FRDM i.MX 8M Plus: the custom-driver overlay is rendered from the
	  board profile and refuses to build until FRDM-GATE-PIR evidence
	  sets the PIR pin; the primary gpio-keys node is merged into the
	  boot DTB by bhp-board-device-tree instead.

	  BeagleBone Black (history): the custom-driver and stock
	  gpio-keys overlays for P9.21 / GPIO0_3.

	  Overlays installed here are not added to the boot flow and have
	  no electrical or wake-cycle verification. Never apply two
	  overlays that claim the same pad.

comment "bhp-presence-sensor needs a Linux kernel"
	depends on !BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
